From d6b60fb97b252271fc0d3fdf265155cc3ca8735b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Krish Paul <me@krishnendu.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 02:55:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Video player: MPEG-4 and H.264 files from the card's
 Video folder

A Video tile under More lists the card's Video folder and plays a file
over the whole panel, turned sideways when it is wider than tall, with
pause, ten-second skips, a progress bar, and the place it was left at
remembered per film. Hardware and remote keys pause and skip while a
film is up.

The decoder is FFmpeg 9.0.2, cross-built static by the Makefile like
FreeType and the audio libraries and cut down to MPEG-4, H.264,
MPEG-1/2 and fixed-point AAC, MP3, MP2 and AC-3. Nothing is scaled and
a file larger than the panel is refused: the X1600 decodes MPEG-4 at
800x450 in about 15 ms a frame and H.264 in about 50, so files are
meant to be converted first with tools/video-convert.sh.

Sound is the clock. The decoder keeps a fifth of a second of it in the
card and a frame is shown when its sample reaches the DAC; when the
core runs short the decoder drops B-frames, then everything but key
frames, before the sound gives way. With nothing over the picture,
frames are converted straight into the off-screen framebuffer page and
the pages swapped, without LVGL copying the panel again.

Shared code touched: audio_external_delay_ms() and
audio_external_start() for an external source that paces itself,
display_direct_page() and display_direct_flip() in main.c, and the
refresh-period helper the Game Boy screen had to itself is now
gui_refresh_period_set() for both pages.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
